comic-story fix log. One block per epoch: train/test brief, settings, score (1-5: look, motion, staging, readability, story, length), flaws seen, fixes made.

== c1  2026-11-17  train: "life of a person with insomnia..." 45 s  |  1 director round  |  STOPPED at 18 min (broken, not slow)
flaws:
- main character never drawn: the template asked for a "lie" pose inside a tall standing box (420x820); a lying figure cannot fit, so all 6 attempts failed "draws outside its box", every shot using her crashed and retried, 5 shots rendered black, and the director round redrew everything into the same wall
- "window" false positives: the banned-global check matched comments and strings ("// bedroom window"), about 12 rejections
- caption pop-in (scale from 0) flagged as "0 px" text
- M3 slips that cost attempts: duplicate const declarations ('shoe', 'line'), unbalanced save/restore
good: kit passed first try with real rooms (background detail check 1.6 passed); supporting character and bed drew fine
fixes (system):
- template: the character box fits every pose (about square, e.g. 760x900); lie = rotated 90 degrees and scaled to the box width
- stage: every previewed state is checked against the box, and the message names the state and the measured extents in box units; small-text check skips text that is still scaling in
- engine: banned globals are looked for in code only (comments and strings stripped; a variable the code declares itself is fine); the run stops right after the assets step if any asset has no valid code, instead of rendering black shots and spending a review round
