== c2  2026-11-17  train: same brief  |  1 director round  |  ~16 min incl. a crash at the end + resume; first part 39 calls / 164k output tokens (input not logged), resume 7 calls / 96k tokens / $0.046
score: look 4, motion 3, staging 3, readability 3, story 3, length 5 (47.2 s)
good: real comic rooms (night bedroom with moon, lamp, 3:07 AM clock; kitchen; office; evening cafe), consistent main character and coworker, speech and thought bubbles, lip-sync, facts from the reference (chronic = 3 nights a week for 3 months after the director fix; CBT first-line; causes list)
flaws:
- lying character placed on the floor in front of the bed, not in it (no back/front layering for things a character sits or lies in)
- empty yellow caption box; a long caption runs off both frame edges; the help banner squeezes a sentence into a strip (illegible)
- the "others" shot paints a plain grey wall over the kit room
- no hopeful outcome shot; hook names the time but no surprising fact
- engine crash after the review: a removed line still had a sound effect (fixed: sfx for missing lines are skipped)
fixes after c2 review (system):
- stage: acting check (template "acting beat: 3.5"): the hero's discrete params (pose, expression, facing, holding) must change, or it must move 30 px, about once per 3.5 s of shot; replayed on c2 it flags exactly the 5 static shots
- stage: a solid opaque fillRect over 30% of the frame drawn after kit.bg is rejected (caught the grey wall in shot 5; no false hits on 8 thyroidectomy shots)
- stage: text must stay inside x 44 to 1036 once fully scaled in (was 8: the clipped "3 nights a week" caption at x 26 to 1054 passed); text squeezed by fillText maxWidth over 12% is rejected
- stage: the hero's drawn box is the union over all previewed states (the lying first state made a standing hero look small)
- template: outcome beat required; one line of 12 to 16 words per shot; set pieces a character lies in get a back/front "layer" param and shots draw back, character, front; arms and hands always visible; supporting person keeps the same proportions; props never over faces; caption box at most 5 words, sized to its text, never empty; sound words away from the speech bubble; never paint walls over kit.bg

